<Base title="About · Rohan Aslam">
  <div class="pt-8">
    <h1 class="h1">About</h1>
    <hr class="rule-heavy mt-3" />
    <div class="prose mt-6">
      <p>
        I'm Rohan Aslam and I live in Scarborough, which means I've spent a meaningful fraction
        of my life on the Lakeshore East line.
      </p>

      <p>
        I studied Communication, Culture, Information and Technology at U of T Mississauga with a
        computer science minor. It's an arts degree that taught me to build things, which sounds
        like a contradiction right up until you have to explain a technical decision to someone
        who doesn't care about the technology.
      </p>

      <p>
        Then five internships. Web development at RBC. Sixteen months on the Experience Design
        and Innovation team at Ontario Teachers'. Design research at the U of T Innovation Hub,
        where I spent a term talking to teachers across Ontario about problems I never would have
        guessed at from a desk. Product at Dye and Durham, on eCore. Then digital transformation
        at Sun Life, building agents in Copilot Studio and dashboards in Power BI, which turned
        into a full time offer on the SunAdvantage team.
      </p>

      <p>
        Somewhere in there I co-founded <a href="/work/smartsyllabus">SmartSyllabus</a> with two
        friends and it stopped being a course project. It's live at smartsyllabus.ca, and it's
        taught me more about strategy than any class did. Mostly because a course project can't
        fail in public.
      </p>

      <p>
        Most weekends I build something small. A Telegram bot that files my thoughts into Notion.
        A pipeline that ranks job postings so I stop scrolling. None of it is impressive on its
        own. It's how I find out whether an idea is any good before I spend three months arguing
        for it.
      </p>

      <p>
        Outside of that I hike. Algonquin, Petroglyphs, and one day trip to Charlevoix that
        involved leaving Scarborough at 3:40 in the morning and getting home twenty six hours
        later. I also help plan events and volunteer rotations in my community, which is project
        management with no budget and no authority. I recommend it to anyone who thinks they're
        good at logistics.
      </p>

      <h2>What I'm looking for</h2>
      <p>
        Strategy and operations roles at startups. The kind of job where working out what matters
        and making it real are the same task. If that's your team,
        <a href="mailto:rohanaslam24@gmail.com">email me</a> or find me on
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/rohanaslam">LinkedIn</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
